From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:13:55 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: don't arm a reset from a setup that
 fails

When brcmf_pcie_setup() fails, it reports the crash with
brcmf_fw_crashed() and then releases the driver. brcmf_fw_crashed()
also arms the bus reset work. brcmf_pcie_remove(), called from
device_release_driver(), drains that work with
brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(); but by then the reset has usually run:
it detached the bus and queued a new firmware request. That request's
brcmf_pcie_setup() then runs while remove frees the chip, and it
dereferences devinfo->ci in the firmware wait loop of
brcmf_pcie_download_fw_nvram():

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 000000000000001c
  pc : brcmf_pcie_setup+0x4d0/0x1008 [brcmfmac]
  Call trace:
   brcmf_pcie_setup+0x4d0/0x1008 [brcmfmac] (P)
   brcmf_fw_request_done+0x144/0x188 [brcmfmac]
   request_firmware_work_func+0x50/0xec

The reset work and the firmware workers stay stuck afterwards.

Block the reset before reporting the crash, as remove does: the driver
is released anyway, so the report keeps its coredump and nothing races
the release.

Found on a Pixel 9a (BCM4383) by suspending with the driver loaded: the
chip doesn't survive s2idle, the hot resume finds the firmware crashed,
the recovery reset's firmware download fails ("FW failed to
initialize"), and the second firmware request crashed as above. With
this change the same sequence ends with "Dongle setup failed", the
driver released, no oops and no task stuck in D state.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index bb70f3bbd..4093e7d51 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2232,6 +2232,13 @@ static void brcmf_pcie_setup(struct device *dev, int ret,
 fail:
 	brcmf_err(bus, "Dongle setup failed\n");
 	brcmf_pcie_bus_console_read(devinfo, true);
+	/*
+	 * The driver is released below, so report the crash (the coredump)
+	 * without arming a recovery reset: brcmf_pcie_remove() would wait for
+	 * that reset, which by then has queued a new firmware request whose
+	 * brcmf_pcie_setup() runs while remove frees the chip.
+	 */
+	brcmf_bus_cancel_reset_work(bus);
 	brcmf_fw_crashed(dev);
 	device_release_driver(dev);
 }
